💡 **SUGGESTION: `_applyImportedEntry` doc comment contradicts the new ordering**

`lib/src/cli/provider_export_command.dart:591-593`, directly above this hunk, still reads:

```dart
/// Applies an imported CUSTOM entry: per-name conflict prompt (keep
/// local / take bundle, never silent overwrite), key write into the
/// entry's slot, registry add, persist, and the switch offer.
```

The body this PR rewrites now deliberately does the opposite: `registry.add` **first** (the reserved-name fails-before-any-key-write guarantee commented at line 637), the key write **second** (lines 645-651), and **no persist at all** in this function — activation and persist were moved to the accepted switch (`_switchToSavedProvider`). All three claims in the doc comment ("key write into the entry's slot, registry add, persist") are now stale.

Suggested rewording:

```dart
/// Applies an imported CUSTOM entry: per-name conflict prompt (keep
/// local / take bundle, never silent overwrite), registry add first (a
/// reserved name fails before any key-slot write), then the key write,
/// and the switch offer — persist happens only at accept, via the switch.
```

Doc-only, no behavioral impact — but it sits 40 lines above the brand-new "Registry add FIRST" inline comment and a future reader will trust the `///` over the code.

